  "limitations": [
    "The checked-in PostgreSQL/RLS/index integration test was not executed because no local PostgreSQL runtime or .env was available. The concurrent index build, restricted-role tenant behavior, populated upgrade, invalid-index recovery, and representative query/build timing remain unverified on the 49-migration chain.",
    "No provider credential, Shopify/Stripe sandbox request, real provider pagination, webhook delivery, gap-repair completeness, provider outage, source-system write, protected staging, or production traffic was exercised.",
    "The endpoint computes independent maxima from immutable source-event metadata. Those timestamps do not prove one shared latest row, normalization success, retained raw evidence, provider completeness, current availability, reconciliation correctness, or financial state.",
    "Source-event metadata can outlive raw-payload retention, and CSV rollback intentionally retains source observation history. Operators must not interpret a watermark as current reconciliation eligibility.",
    "A provider-skewed future source timestamp remains visible. Separate bounded freshness telemetry classifies it; this view does not clamp it or make it health authority.",
    "The additive index requires production backup, capacity, lock/timeout, WAL/replica, interruption, compatibility, and rollback rehearsal. New API/web images must not be deployed before the migration is ready.",
    "The source-event aggregation still needs representative-volume EXPLAIN/ANALYZE and tenant timing review. No latency, throughput, SLO, completeness, reliability, or production-readiness claim is made."
  ]
